# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Virtual envs (.venv-* = a scratch environment, e.g. the no-SDK proof for row 7.15)
.venv*/

# Secrets never enter the repo (engine invariant; secrets resolve from env at runtime)
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
secrets/
credentials.json

# age identities (row 7.22). The ENCRYPTED tenant.secrets.enc.yaml is safe to
# commit and is deliberately NOT ignored; the identity that opens it lives on
# the box and nowhere else, so every shape it is usually written in is ignored
# here whatever directory somebody runs age-keygen in.
keys.txt
*.agekey
age/

# Local ledger workspaces (per-deployment git repos live outside the code repo)
.ledger/
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite3-journal

# The auditor's own store (working memory, rebuildable by re-running the audit)
.auditor/

# The model seat's scratch directories (issue #265): one per call, swept when
# the call returns, with scratch-log.jsonl the record that outlives them. Here
# for the same reason .ledger/ and .auditor/ are: the freshness guard refuses a
# checkout with untracked files, and the default root is beside the run.
.llm-scratch/

# Runner session transcripts (row 7.17), when nothing names a root: beside the
# run, like .llm-scratch/ above. The triage lane names its own under the stage.
.runner-transcripts/

# Data trees `engine init` creates beside tenants/ (the demo's is demo-data/):
# inboxes, filed documents, reports. Never part of the code repo.
/*-data/

# Claude Code tooling: agent worktrees live under .claude/worktrees/ inside the
# repo; untracked, they made the 06:00 headless triage see a dirty dev tree and
# skip every fire since it went live (2026-09-02 through 09-04; added 2026-09-04)
.claude/

# OS
.DS_Store

# coverage.py data (held 317 absolute paths when it was tracked; removed at extraction gate 2)
.coverage
.coverage.*

# CI checks the private tenant token list out here (never committed)
.private-tenant/
